The following quells the warning, so add it to your pull request:

diff --git a/tests/testrig.c b/tests/testrig.c
index 250b7e25..99d8ce8f 100644
--- a/tests/testrig.c
+++ b/tests/testrig.c
@@ -401,7 +401,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])

     if (retcode == RIG_OK)
     {
-        printf("rig_get_mode: mode = %i \n", rmode);
+        printf("rig_get_mode: mode = %lli \n", rmode);
     }
     else
     {

It's re-using IC-7300 routines and so far there's nothing really custom about it other than the freq ranges and modes.We found the IC-7300 to be highly compatible.  There are several places in the code where co-existent rig_caps in one file exist...it minimizes the # of lines of code and forces you to realize that one rig is related to another.If we have to start coding custom routines for the IC9700 I would extract it.
de Mike W9MDB





