@mdblack98 Yes, it is definitely one of the rarely used features, but is definitely useful with remote control applications, such as the one I'm building.

The problem with Icom rigs is that it is not possible to tell the frequency range, as it seems to vary between rigs and it also depends on other settings in the rig, such as waterfall span in IC-7300, like @N0NB mentioned.

I was wondering if we could leave the current `RIG_LEVEL_NOTCHF` as it is (as many rigs do support specifying the filter using an absolute frequency) and introduce a new level for rigs like Icom that do not specify any unit for the notch filter settings. That new level could then use a float value with either range of -1..1 or 0..1. Not sure what that should be called... `RIG_LEVEL_NOTCHF_SIMPLE`? Ideas? :)

OK...so try the attached.  Now that we know what to expect we can check for it.
de Mike W9MDB







