The root cause is that `rig_set_split_freq()` trusts `rig_get_freq()` to return accurate data, but the cache can be corrupted when VFOA/MAIN share cache slots with the RX VFO during split operations.

Recommendation: Remove the optimization

In `src/rig.c`, around line 4700, remove or disable the "skip if same" check:

```
  // REMOVE THIS BLOCK - cache can be stale/corrupted during split
  #if 0
      rig_get_freq(rig, tx_vfo, &tfreq);
      if (tfreq == tx_freq)
      {
          rig_debug(RIG_DEBUG_TRACE, "%s: freq set not needed\n", __func__);
          ELAPSED2;
          RETURNFUNC2(RIG_OK);
      }
  #endif
```

Rationale: The optimization saves one serial command but causes silent failures when cache is wrong. Most rigs handle "set to current freq" gracefully, and the time saved is negligible compared to the bug impact.

