@KJ5HST Yes, more or less what you've described. I'll post my design here within a couple of days here. I still need to iterate on a couple of things, but essentially this is an add-on to Hamlib to support UDP streaming of audio and I/Q data - or if linking directly to Hamlib, an application can directly use a backend to stream audio or I/Q data in a "standardized" format. This includes a ring buffer design internally and there's of course a proposal for the UDP protocol too.

The control commands (when using Hamlib over the network, e.g. rigctld) would be integrated into the existing Hamlib TCP protocol with additional commands.

