I read some more of the code, and I think what you're seeing is by design.  Some comments in function `kenwood_set_mode()` -

    // we won't set opposite VFO if the mode is the same as requested
    // setting VFOB mode requires split modifications which cause VFO flashing
    // this should generally work unless the user changes mode on VFOB
    // in which case VFOB won't get mode changed until restart

so hamlib will only set the TX VFO mode the first time a mode is called for.  After that it just assumes it still retains the same mode setting, and will only set it again if the RX mode changes. This is for two reasons; as above, changing it each transmission would cause the display to flicker back and forth between to two VFOs, and VFO switching takes a while.  A full cycle could take on the order of seconds on rigs of that era, and that's a good part of an FT8 cycle - even worse for FT4 (or FT2!)

So let's make sure WSJT-X is happy with the current operation, and I think we'll have to leave it at that.

