> A design question rather than a complaint. For a relaying consumer like mine — I re-originate the audio onto another multi-point wire, so conversion cost lands in a latency budget I care about — is require_native = 1 the intended mechanism to guarantee a byte-shuttle, or do you expect consumers to accept conversion and read rig_stream_get_conversions() for reporting?

If I understand your case correctly, the `require_native = 1` flag is meant for your use-case: it will make opening of a stream fail if the backend cannot provide the sample/data format natively. You should be able to see the natively-supported formats via `\stream_caps` (the `native_*` keys) and pick one from there. The flag will ensure you will not get any conversion applied.
